# Frontend-only engineering

All solutions are **frontend-engineered**. `predictions-backend` (Java/Spring) exists **only as a reference** so agents can learn live API shapes, DTOs, cookies, and error codes.

## Do

- Implement features, mappings, fallbacks, and empty states in `predictions-frontend/`
- Read backend DTOs/controllers to discover JSON field names — then consume them in JS
- If the API is missing a field, use what exists, client fallbacks, and optionally `docs/proposals/` — do not patch the server

## Do not

- Create, edit, delete, or commit anything under `predictions-backend/` (including `*.java`, yaml, migrations, tests)
- “Just add a field” to a DTO or mapper because the UI needs it
- Run backend codegen, OpenAPI regeneration that writes Java, or Flyway migrations

```js
// ❌ BAD — changing Java so standings include avatar
// LeagueMember.java: private String avatar;

// ✅ GOOD — consume whatever the payload already has
<Avatar name={m.username} src={m.avatar || m.profilePicture || m.profilePictureUrl} />
```
